---
// Project: ORBIT. Type: interface plus code, read top to bottom.
// Idea, TM-4715 section 2: "a configuration-driven web interface dynamically adapts navigation hierarchies, controller
// displays, and visualization parameters to heterogeneous HVAC configurations without requiring separate interface
// development." The pairing follows TM-4715 Fig. 6 (YAML configurations beside their charts).
// Labels and sources:
//   the six code lines            example-config-files/example_YAML-config.yml in the ORBIT repository, "chart configs"
//                                  (chart 1, chart type: line, selected variables 1 to 3); the same block as TM-4715 Fig. 6
//   rendered by the web interface SimBuild 2026: "enabling the web interface to automatically render appropriate dashboards"
//   web application               README: "Web application"
//   Chart 1, Line Chart           TM-4715 Fig. 6 (the chart header in the web application)
//   legend names                  the YAML variables; line styles from the same file's "line dash: dashdot / dot / solid"
// Left out on purpose: the file's operator name, image URL and building ID, and its color keys (the chart uses the
// site colors). Illustrative: the curves, with no values.
// Fine-line drawing (classes .dgf in global.css), in the 300 x 356 frame shared by the four project drawings.
// Motion (projects.py in research/compare-2026-10-30-theme-drawings/tools; transform and opacity only, generated
// <style> below): code becomes interface. Intro, once in view: the six YAML lines type in, the arrow grows, the
// browser window appears, the axes draw, the three curves draw left to right. Loop, 8 s: line 4 and the heating
// setpoint take the focus (the other curves dim), then line 5 and the cooling setpoint, then line 6 and the zone
// temperature; a read point rides the curve in focus. Static without JS or with reduced motion.
---
